      "chunk_idx": 1,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Background.",
      "token_count": 4,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Background."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00002",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 2,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "Maintaining its position at #1 in the Top Ten, 100% of the applications tested were found to have some form of broken access control.\n\nNotable CWEs included are *CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor*, *CWE-201: Exposure of Sensitive Information Through Sent Data*, *CWE-918 Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)*, and *CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)*.\n\nThis category has the highest number of occurrences in the contributed data, and second highest number of related CVEs.",
      "token_count": 112,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Background."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00003",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 3,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
