      "chunk_idx": 5,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Description.",
      "token_count": 4,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Description."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00006",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 6,
      "chunk_type": "mixed",
      "text_content": "Access control enforces policy such that users cannot act outside of their intended permissions.\n\nFailures typically lead to unauthorized information disclosure, modification or destruction of all data, or performing a business function outside the user's limits.\n\nCommon access control vulnerabilities include:\n\n* Violation of the principle of least privilege, commonly known as deny by default, where access should only be granted for particular capabilities, roles, or users, but is available to anyone.\n\n* Bypassing access control checks by modifying the URL (parameter tampering or force browsing), internal application state, or the HTML page, or by using an attack tool that modifies API requests.\n\n* Permitting viewing or editing someone else's account by providing its unique identifier (insecure direct object references)\n* An accessible API with missing access controls for POST, PUT, and DELETE.\n\n* Elevation of privilege.\n\nActing as a user without being logged in or or gaining privileges beyond those expected of the logged in user (e.g.\n\nadmin access).\n\n* Metadata manipulation, such as replaying or tampering with a JSON Web Token (JWT) access control token, a cookie or hidden field manipulated to elevate privileges, or abusing JWT invalidation.\n\n* CORS misconfiguration allows API access from unauthorized or untrusted origins.\n\n* Force browsing (guessing URLs) to authenticated pages as an unauthenticated user or to privileged pages as a standard user.",
      "token_count": 264,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Description."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00007",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 7,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## How to prevent.",
      "token_count": 6,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "How to prevent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00008",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 8,
      "chunk_type": "mixed",
      "text_content": "Access control is only effective when implemented in trusted server-side code or serverless APIs, where the attacker cannot modify the access control check or metadata.\n\n* Except for public resources, deny by default.\n\n* Implement access control mechanisms once and reuse them throughout the application, including minimizing Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) usage.\n\n* Model access controls should enforce record ownership rather than allowing users to create, read, update, or delete any record.\n\n* Unique application business limit requirements should be enforced by domain models.\n\n* Disable web server directory listing and ensure file metadata (e.g., .git) and backup files are not present within web roots.\n\n* Log access control failures, alert admins when appropriate (e.g., repeated failures).\n\n* Implement rate limits on API and controller access to minimize the harm from automated attack tooling.\n\n* Stateful session identifiers should be invalidated on the server after logout.\n\nStateless JWT tokens should be short-lived to minimize the window of opportunity for an attacker.\n\nFor longer-lived JWTs, consider using refresh tokens and following OAuth standards to revoke access.\n\n* Use well-established toolkits or patterns that provide simple, declarative access controls.\n\nDevelopers and QA staff should include functional access control in their unit and integration tests.",
      "token_count": 249,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "How to prevent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00009",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 9,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Example attack scenarios.",
      "token_count": 6,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00010",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 10,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "**Scenario #1:** The application uses unverified data in an SQL call that is accessing account information:",
      "token_count": 23,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00011",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 11,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\npstmt.setString(1, request.getParameter(\"acct\"));\nResultSet results = pstmt.executeQuery( );\n```",
      "token_count": 31,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00012",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 12,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "An attacker can simply modify the browser's 'acct' parameter to send any desired account number.\n\nIf not correctly verified, the attacker can access any user's account.",
      "token_count": 35,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00013",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 13,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\nhttps://example.com/app/accountInfo?acct=notmyacct\n```",
      "token_count": 21,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00014",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 14,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "**Scenario #2:** An attacker simply forces browsers to target URLs.\n\nAdmin rights are required for access to the admin page.",
      "token_count": 28,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00015",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 15,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\nhttps://example.com/app/getappInfo\nhttps://example.com/app/admin_getappInfo\n```",
      "token_count": 28,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00016",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 16,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "If an unauthenticated user can access either page, it's a flaw.\n\nIf a non-admin can access the admin page, this is a flaw.\n\n**Scenario #3:** An application puts all of their access control in their front-end.\n\nWhile the attacker cannot get to `https://example.com/app/admin_getappInfo` due to JavaScript code running in the browser, they can simply execute:",
      "token_count": 86,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00017",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 17,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\n$ curl https://example.com/app/admin_getappInfo\n```",
      "token_count": 19,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00018",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 18,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "from the command line.",
      "token_count": 5,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2025 Broken Access Control",
        "Example attack scenarios."
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422_c00019",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_d6ebc4e65422",
      "chunk_idx": 19,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
